{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "manifestId": "follow-demo",
  "manifestRevision": 1,
  "description": "Matcher test phrases for demo/manifest.json (PRD §15.2-15.3). Calibrate only on \"rehearsal\"; score \"heldOut\" once, untouched.",
  "semantics": {
    "cases": "Each case is scored independently from an Overview state with nothing focused.",
    "expect": "FOCUS/REVEAL/COMPARE/HOLD use CanvasAction names. REVEAL implies its concept is focused. COMPARE on the comparison concept means composing its approved endpoints.",
    "settling": "In sequences, settling: true marks the first utterance on a new topic: HOLD or the expected action are both acceptable (two-consecutive-match rule).",
    "manual": "kind \"manual\" is a presenter action that enters manual hold; kind \"control\" with \"resume\" clears it and starts a fresh decision window.",
    "silence": "kind \"silence\" is durationMs of no speech; the canvas must not move."
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "r01",
      "split": "rehearsal",
      "kind": "paraphrase",
      "text": "The trouble with a normal deck is that you've committed to the running order before you've said a word.",
      "expect": {
        "action": "FOCUS",
        "conceptId": "problem"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "r02",
      "split": "rehearsal",
      "kind": "paraphrase",
      "text": "You know that moment when somebody asks about slide three and you're frantically clicking back?",
      "expect": {
        "action": "FOCUS",
        "conceptId": "problem"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "r03",
      "split": "rehearsal",
      "kind": "paraphrase",
      "text": "Slides basically force you down one single path through the material.",
      "expect": {
        "action": "FOCUS",
        "conceptId": "problem"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "r04",
      "split": "rehearsal",
      "kind": "paraphrase",
      "text": "Honestly, most talks end up with the presenter working for the slides.",
      "expect": {
        "action": "FOCUS",
        "conceptId": "problem"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "r05",
      "split": "rehearsal",
      "kind": "paraphrase",
      "text": "We wanted to turn that relationship completely upside down.",
      "expect": {
        "action": "FOCUS",
        "conceptId": "reversal"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "r06",
      "split": "rehearsal",
      "kind": "paraphrase",
      "text": "Instead of me keeping up with the deck, the visuals keep up with me.",
      "expect": {
        "action": "FOCUS",
        "conceptId": "reversal"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "r07",
      "split": "rehearsal",
      "kind": "paraphrase",
      "text": "There's nothing to stick to, I just talk and the right thing shows up.",
      "expect": {
        "action": "FOCUS",
        "conceptId": "reversal"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "r08",
      "split": "rehearsal",
      "kind": "paraphrase",
      "text": "So the idea is that the talk drives the screen, not the other way around.",
      "expect": {
        "action": "FOCUS",
        "conceptId": "reversal"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "r09",
      "split": "rehearsal",
      "kind": "paraphrase",
      "text": "Under the hood there are really four stages.",
      "expect": {
        "action": "FOCUS",
        "conceptId": "pipeline"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "r10",
      "split": "rehearsal",
      "kind": "paraphrase",
      "text": "Let me explain what's happening behind the scenes while I speak.",
      "expect": {
        "action": "FOCUS",
        "conceptId": "pipeline"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "r11",
      "split": "rehearsal",
      "kind": "paraphrase",
      "text": "It's a loop: hear me, transcribe me, figure out which idea I mean, and draw it.",
      "expect": {
        "action": "FOCUS",
        "conceptId": "pipeline"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "r12",
      "split": "rehearsal",
      "kind": "paraphrase",
      "text": "Here is the chain of steps that gets my voice onto the screen.",
      "expect": {
        "action": "FOCUS",
        "conceptId": "pipeline"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "r13",
      "split": "rehearsal",
      "kind": "paraphrase",
      "text": "It goes by what I mean, not by the exact words I happen to use.",
      "expect": {
        "action": "FOCUS",
        "conceptId": "matching"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "r14",
      "split": "rehearsal",
      "kind": "paraphrase",
      "text": "If it can't tell what I'm on about, it simply doesn't move.",
      "expect": {
        "action": "FOCUS",
        "conceptId": "matching"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "r15",
      "split": "rehearsal",
      "kind": "paraphrase",
      "text": "How does it decide which idea I am referring to? By meaning.",
      "expect": {
        "action": "FOCUS",
        "conceptId": "matching"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "r16",
      "split": "rehearsal",
      "kind": "paraphrase",
      "text": "I don't need to memorise any phrasing for this to work.",
      "expect": {
        "action": "FOCUS",
        "conceptId": "matching"
